WEBVTT

00:17.184 --> 00:19.729
-[Boyd] Previously on From...
-[townspeople screaming]

00:19.812 --> 00:22.273
-[gun firing]
-Abby, stop! No!

00:22.356 --> 00:23.691
[gasps]

00:28.654 --> 00:30.281
Still seeing things
that aren't there?

00:30.364 --> 00:32.783
No. No, just the one time.

00:32.867 --> 00:34.577
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:34.660 --> 00:37.121
[gasps]

00:37.204 --> 00:38.330
I've been here before.

00:38.414 --> 00:40.040
Many, many times.

00:40.124 --> 00:42.293
I was Victor's mother.

00:42.376 --> 00:44.420
[Victor] Last time, you brought
a boy and a girl,

00:44.503 --> 00:46.213
and everyone died,
but not the boy.

00:46.297 --> 00:47.882
You're here with a boy
and a girl again,

00:47.965 --> 00:49.175
and the Man in Yellow is back.

00:49.258 --> 00:51.010
-Mom, what does that mean?
-No, it's fine.

00:51.093 --> 00:52.887
-You have to be prepared, Ethan.
-Hey, Victor.

00:52.970 --> 00:54.889
-You have to know what's coming.
-No, Victor. You need to stop!

00:54.972 --> 00:56.724
What's wrong with you?

00:56.807 --> 00:58.267
That thing I carried
inside me,

00:58.350 --> 01:00.853
I still feel it,
like we're connected.

01:00.936 --> 01:03.647
Part of me feels
what he feels.

01:09.069 --> 01:10.446
Oh, no.

01:12.198 --> 01:13.824
[roars]

01:13.908 --> 01:15.618
No!

01:15.701 --> 01:17.119
You wanna go down
in those tunnels,

01:17.203 --> 01:18.954
where those things live
because you think

01:19.038 --> 01:20.998
the bones of those children
are buried down there?

01:21.081 --> 01:24.210
Yes!
What if the bones

01:24.293 --> 01:27.170
are what anchor the spirits
of those children here?

01:27.254 --> 01:30.174
Tell me what the right version
of this plan looks like.

01:30.257 --> 01:32.134
I'm not entirely sure yet.

01:32.218 --> 01:35.179
Here's to the resiliency
of the human spirit.

01:35.262 --> 01:37.723
Let's be resilient together.

01:39.475 --> 01:42.520
Have you ever wondered if
maybe this is all just a dream?

01:43.938 --> 01:47.358
[monitor beeping]

01:47.441 --> 01:50.110
He's back.
Blink twice if you can hear me.

01:50.194 --> 01:51.402
Dad.

01:51.487 --> 01:53.280
-V--
-Dad, stay with me.

01:53.364 --> 01:54.949
Henry!
[snaps]

01:55.032 --> 01:55.950
Hey.

01:57.952 --> 02:00.246
[whispering
indistinct incantation]

02:00.329 --> 02:02.623
It's time to play.

02:02.706 --> 02:05.334
-[roars]
-I know you're still inside!

02:05.417 --> 02:06.710
[roars]

02:06.794 --> 02:08.127
[roars in pain]

02:08.211 --> 02:11.006
[screaming]
What the fuck just happened?!

02:11.090 --> 02:12.675
[weeping]

02:15.761 --> 02:17.680
[chattering]

02:20.432 --> 02:23.310
We're sure he's actually
dead this time, right?

02:23.394 --> 02:25.688
He was dead before.

02:25.771 --> 02:27.314
Anybody hurt?

02:27.398 --> 02:29.233
Steve got pretty banged up.

02:29.316 --> 02:31.360
It would've been a lot worse
if it wasn't for Elgin.

02:31.443 --> 02:32.319
Elgin?

02:32.403 --> 02:33.821
He's the one who stabbed it--

02:33.904 --> 02:35.739
I mean, him.

02:35.823 --> 02:39.493
Stop telling me to calm down!
We're not fucking safe!

02:39.577 --> 02:41.829
Hey, will you just
take it outside?

02:43.956 --> 02:46.125
Hey, Donna,
you should be in bed.

02:46.208 --> 02:47.293
No, no, no, no.
[stammers]

02:47.376 --> 02:51.255
I'm fine.
This is more important.

02:51.338 --> 02:53.632
People are just starting
to realize that talismans

02:53.716 --> 02:56.051
won't protect them
against everything.

02:56.135 --> 02:58.012
We'll manage.
Just... you figure out

02:58.095 --> 03:00.973
how to get the bones without
getting half the town killed.

03:01.056 --> 03:02.474
Did the totem work?

03:03.893 --> 03:05.311
Sorry?

03:05.394 --> 03:06.520
The totems from
the settlement.

03:06.604 --> 03:08.606
You said that
you were gonna see

03:08.689 --> 03:11.567
if they could hurt the monsters
that come out at night.

03:11.650 --> 03:12.902
Did it work?

03:12.985 --> 03:14.153
No.

03:16.030 --> 03:17.114
That's too bad.

03:17.197 --> 03:18.240
Yeah.

03:18.324 --> 03:20.659
Dad?

03:20.743 --> 03:22.870
Uh, can you come
upstairs for a second?

03:22.953 --> 03:24.454
-Excuse me.
-And, uh,

03:24.538 --> 03:26.040
Donna, you should probably
come too, if you're up for it.

03:29.418 --> 03:31.128
Uh, what do we
do with the body?

03:35.299 --> 03:36.800
Burn it.

03:42.598 --> 03:44.558
Okay, so, you're saying...

03:46.518 --> 03:48.687
...that you saw
Kenny in trouble.

03:50.189 --> 03:53.067
Look, I didn't
just see him, Boyd.

03:53.150 --> 03:55.402
It's like I was there.

03:55.486 --> 03:57.905
I was seeing
through his eyes.

03:57.988 --> 04:00.074
Through...
And you think

04:00.157 --> 04:03.243
that you're the reason
that thing didn't kill Kenny.

04:03.327 --> 04:05.704
I don't think, Boyd;
I know I was.

04:05.788 --> 04:07.539
-Uh--
-[Ellis] And there's more.

04:08.999 --> 04:10.459
Show 'em.

04:10.542 --> 04:12.252
Show us what?

04:16.089 --> 04:18.091
After I connected
with that thing, I felt...

04:20.886 --> 04:22.930
...I don't know how
to describe it.

04:23.013 --> 04:25.307
I felt something go...

04:25.391 --> 04:27.893
cold inside me.

04:29.269 --> 04:30.604
Okay.

04:32.106 --> 04:33.065
[sighs]

04:33.148 --> 04:34.942
Wh...?

04:35.025 --> 04:37.778
This morning I saw this.

04:37.861 --> 04:40.364
[ominous music playing]

04:50.207 --> 04:55.087
["Que Sera, Sera (Whatever Will
Be, Will Be)" plays]

04:59.967 --> 05:04.763
♪ When I was just a little boy ♪

05:04.847 --> 05:07.266
♪ I asked my father ♪

05:07.349 --> 05:08.892
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

05:11.020 --> 05:13.313
♪ "Will I be handsome?" ♪

05:13.397 --> 05:15.774
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

05:15.858 --> 05:19.820
♪ Here's what he said to me ♪

05:19.903 --> 05:22.781
♪ Que sera sera ♪

05:24.116 --> 05:27.327
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

05:28.996 --> 05:33.082
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

05:33.167 --> 05:35.878
♪ Que sera sera ♪

05:38.172 --> 05:41.050
♪ What will be will be ♪

05:50.517 --> 05:55.314
♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪

05:55.397 --> 05:57.733
♪ They ask their father ♪

05:57.816 --> 06:01.487
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

06:01.570 --> 06:03.989
♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪

06:04.073 --> 06:06.408
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

06:06.492 --> 06:08.827
♪ I tell them tenderly ♪

06:10.454 --> 06:13.040
♪ Que sera sera ♪

06:14.625 --> 06:17.795
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

06:19.630 --> 06:23.509
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

06:23.592 --> 06:26.053
♪ Que sera sera ♪

06:28.680 --> 06:31.600
♪ What will be will be ♪

06:33.936 --> 06:36.730
♪ Que sera sera ♪

06:51.453 --> 06:52.496
[Tabitha] Ethan?

06:56.875 --> 06:58.377
Whatcha doing?

07:00.170 --> 07:01.463
Drawing.

07:06.093 --> 07:08.554
Victor always said that
the pictures remember.

07:09.930 --> 07:11.765
So, when everyone dies

07:11.849 --> 07:15.769
and I'm here by myself,
I don't want to forget anyone.

07:18.021 --> 07:19.314
I know.

07:21.817 --> 07:25.320
What Victor said yesterday,
he was upset.

07:25.404 --> 07:26.780
I know.

07:26.864 --> 07:28.699
What happened
to him was awful,

07:28.782 --> 07:31.243
but that doesn't mean
that's gonna happen to you.

07:31.326 --> 07:33.328
He said I needed
to be prepared,

07:33.412 --> 07:34.913
so I'm getting prepared.

07:44.256 --> 07:46.216
[Ellis]
Okay. Come on.

07:52.514 --> 07:54.433
I'll meet
you guys down there.

07:54.516 --> 07:57.436
And, hey,
we're gonna figure this out.

07:59.313 --> 08:00.522
I know.

08:00.606 --> 08:01.982
Okay.

08:11.825 --> 08:14.995
What--
What am I looking at here?

08:15.078 --> 08:18.248
It's-- It's a model
of the tunnels.

08:18.332 --> 08:20.876
I understand that.
But why is having

08:20.959 --> 08:25.130
a model better
than drawing a map?

08:25.214 --> 08:26.673
I put a lot
of work into this.

08:26.757 --> 08:28.800
It's not a fucking
science fair, Jade!

08:28.884 --> 08:31.136
Oh, for fuck's sake!
All right, you know what?

08:31.220 --> 08:33.096
This model
incorporates everything,

08:33.179 --> 08:34.806
everything
we know about the tunnels,

08:34.890 --> 08:36.975
everything I got from
being down there myself,

08:37.058 --> 08:38.936
everything Victor
and Tabitha could give me.

08:39.019 --> 08:41.563
The path you took, right?
From the root cellar...

08:41.647 --> 08:42.648
Okay.

08:42.731 --> 08:44.232
Okay, well, given all that,

08:44.316 --> 08:46.568
I got a few different scenarios
for how we can do this,

08:46.652 --> 08:50.447
ranging on a sliding scale
of safety and complexity.

08:50.530 --> 08:53.242
So, you wanna hear the simple
but super dangerous ones first,

08:53.325 --> 08:54.326
or should I start
with the safer,

08:54.409 --> 08:56.245
but more complex and...

08:56.328 --> 08:57.496
possibly impossible ones?

09:00.916 --> 09:03.210
This is the chamber where
the bones are buried, right?

09:03.293 --> 09:04.294
Correct.

09:04.378 --> 09:06.421
And this tunnel,

09:06.505 --> 09:08.715
this is the only way in
or out of that chamber?

09:08.799 --> 09:10.217
Yes.

09:11.343 --> 09:12.511
We don't have a plan.

09:14.096 --> 09:16.014
Well, wait, wait. He hasn't even
had a chance--

09:16.098 --> 09:18.308
Hey, when I was in the army,
we'd call something like this

09:18.392 --> 09:20.394
a shooting gallery,

09:20.477 --> 09:22.271
because once
the enemy's inside,

09:22.354 --> 09:24.898
we are fish
in a fuckin' barrel.

09:24.982 --> 09:27.442
Even if we can get past those
things without waking them up,

09:27.526 --> 09:30.404
we get into the chamber,
we dig up the bones,

09:30.487 --> 09:33.991
what happens when they
wake up while we're in there?

09:34.074 --> 09:37.786
What happens when they block our
only exit out of that chamber?

09:40.163 --> 09:41.623
You need to do better.

09:41.707 --> 09:43.333
[scoffs] How?

09:43.417 --> 09:45.669
I don't know.
I'm not the genius.

09:45.752 --> 09:46.962
Figure it out.

09:49.089 --> 09:50.882
Sure. While I'm at it,
why don't I just build

09:50.966 --> 09:53.051
a fucking hot air balloon
and fly us all out of here?

09:53.135 --> 09:54.428
That'd be great.

10:04.479 --> 10:05.439
[door opens, closes]

10:07.399 --> 10:08.775
Hey!

10:10.819 --> 10:12.654
You didn't even listen
to what he had to say.

10:12.738 --> 10:14.531
I didn't need to.

10:14.614 --> 10:16.366
Kenny, you never go
into a hostile space

10:16.450 --> 10:18.660
without a secondary
exit, period. Okay?

10:18.744 --> 10:21.288
I got it.
So, what do we do?

10:21.371 --> 10:23.332
We already told people
that finding those bones

10:23.415 --> 10:25.083
might be the key to
getting everyone home.

10:25.167 --> 10:27.461
Maybe we go on
a scouting mission.

10:27.544 --> 10:29.504
Take one or two people
down into the tunnels,

10:29.588 --> 10:30.839
see if there's
a crack or a crevice

10:30.922 --> 10:32.507
in that chamber
that we missed somehow.

10:32.591 --> 10:35.218
'Kay. If there's not?

10:36.845 --> 10:38.972
I don't know.

10:39.056 --> 10:42.351
Listen, if we're gonna do this,
we have to do it right.

10:42.434 --> 10:43.977
I'm not gonna lead people
down there, and I can't--

10:44.061 --> 10:45.187
[gun firing]

10:48.899 --> 10:50.859
Boyd?

10:50.942 --> 10:52.027
What's wrong?

10:52.110 --> 10:54.029
What? Nothing. I...

10:56.114 --> 10:57.491
Uh,
I gotta go to the clinic.

10:57.574 --> 10:59.368
I told Ellis
I'd meet them up there.

10:59.451 --> 11:01.036
Is Fatima okay?

11:01.119 --> 11:02.913
I don't know.

11:14.424 --> 11:16.843
Henry.
You need something?

11:16.927 --> 11:18.970
I, um...

11:19.054 --> 11:21.223
What's going on over there?

11:21.306 --> 11:23.517
Boyd wants to go through
everything in storage.

11:23.600 --> 11:25.644
Well, what are
they looking for?

11:25.727 --> 11:28.605
Anything to do with that
yellow suit Victor found?

11:28.688 --> 11:29.773
Oh.

11:31.817 --> 11:32.818
You okay?

11:33.902 --> 11:35.612
I need something to do.

11:35.695 --> 11:37.614
I've been, uh...

11:37.697 --> 11:40.700
Well, I've been
drinking a bit lately.

11:40.784 --> 11:41.952
I think it's starting to...

11:42.035 --> 11:43.787
Hm.

11:43.870 --> 11:48.290
Anyway, I figured if
I could keep myself occupied...

11:48.375 --> 11:50.419
Mm.

11:50.502 --> 11:52.796
Um, I'm not too bad
in a kitchen, if you--

11:52.879 --> 11:54.881
How 'bout you give me
a hand with lunch?

11:54.965 --> 11:55.924
I'd like that. Thank you.

11:56.007 --> 11:56.967
Okay.

11:57.050 --> 11:58.260
Okay.

11:58.343 --> 11:59.803
[Joni Mitchell "Blue"
playing on jukebox]

12:01.680 --> 12:03.890
Ah, don't worry,
you'll get used to that.

12:03.974 --> 12:05.350
Come on.

12:05.434 --> 12:07.477
[Joni Mitchell "Blue"
playing on jukebox]

12:07.561 --> 12:09.646
[Joni Mitchell "Blue"
playing on car stereo]

12:09.729 --> 12:11.481
It does that sometimes.

12:11.565 --> 12:14.317
That tape's been
stuck in there for years.

12:14.401 --> 12:17.362
"Blue" was Miranda's
favorite song.

12:17.446 --> 12:19.448
♪ ...tattoos ♪

12:19.531 --> 12:21.825
♪ You know I've been ♪

12:21.908 --> 12:23.368
♪ To sea before ♪

12:32.919 --> 12:36.131
It never used to
be like this, you know.

12:37.966 --> 12:40.969
It was always scary,

12:41.052 --> 12:42.429
but this...

12:45.056 --> 12:47.309
I really hope Boyd's right
about getting those bones.

12:48.393 --> 12:49.352
Me, too.

13:06.119 --> 13:07.412
[door opens]

13:17.923 --> 13:19.049
[knocking]

13:23.220 --> 13:24.971
Who is it?

13:25.055 --> 13:26.473
[Tabitha]
Open the door, Victor.

13:37.192 --> 13:39.486
Tell him it's not true.

13:41.279 --> 13:42.614
Which part?

13:42.697 --> 13:44.366
The part about him
being here alone.

13:44.449 --> 13:46.159
Tell him
it's not gonna happen.

13:46.243 --> 13:48.537
I can't do that.

13:48.620 --> 13:52.165
Victor,
you don't understand.

13:52.249 --> 13:53.959
It's not helping;
it's scaring him.

13:55.377 --> 13:57.420
Will you teach me?

13:57.504 --> 13:59.047
What?

13:59.130 --> 14:03.760
I want him to teach me how
to survive when I'm alone.

14:03.843 --> 14:06.096
You're not going
to be here alone, Ethan!

14:06.179 --> 14:08.974
You don't know that.

14:09.057 --> 14:11.101
What he said
yesterday was true.

14:11.184 --> 14:14.312
Miranda was here
with him and Eloise.

14:14.396 --> 14:16.231
Now, you're here
with me and Julie.

14:16.314 --> 14:18.441
So what? That doesn't
mean anything!

14:18.525 --> 14:19.818
It might.

14:19.901 --> 14:22.237
It won't be as scary
if I know what to do.

14:22.320 --> 14:23.530
Please.

14:25.824 --> 14:27.158
It's a good idea.

14:33.039 --> 14:34.374
Okay. Fine.

14:45.093 --> 14:46.094
[Kristi] Okay, yeah.

14:46.177 --> 14:48.221
I'm not seeing
any internal damage.

14:48.305 --> 14:50.724
All due respect,
you didn't see the baby either.

14:50.807 --> 14:52.183
Ellis!

14:52.267 --> 14:53.977
No, he's right.

14:54.060 --> 14:56.313
There's not much I can
tell you other than that,

14:56.396 --> 14:58.690
physically, you're not in
any immediate danger.

14:58.773 --> 15:00.734
So, what is it, then?

15:00.817 --> 15:02.694
Well, I mean,
if we were anywhere but here,

15:02.777 --> 15:04.988
I would say those
are varicose veins

15:05.071 --> 15:07.991
from abdominal distension,
but we're here, so...

15:08.074 --> 15:12.162
we are well beyond
a standard diagnosis.

15:12.245 --> 15:13.288
[sighs]

15:17.917 --> 15:21.338
Those things,
you said they used to be human.

15:22.881 --> 15:24.382
When you did the autopsy,

15:24.466 --> 15:26.760
you said all the organs
inside were human.

15:28.219 --> 15:29.929
Is it possible that

15:30.013 --> 15:31.431
I'm turning
into one of them?

15:31.514 --> 15:32.432
No.

15:34.392 --> 15:36.686
No, that's...

15:36.770 --> 15:38.063
That's not what's happening.

15:38.146 --> 15:39.606
Tell her-- tell her
that's not what's happening.

15:39.689 --> 15:40.857
Can you make it stop?

15:40.940 --> 15:42.901
Ellis, we don't even
know what it is.

15:42.984 --> 15:45.987
It might also
not be a bad thing.

15:46.071 --> 15:47.072
Excuse me?

15:47.155 --> 15:48.365
Kenny is alive because of this;

15:48.448 --> 15:49.991
she saved his life.

15:50.075 --> 15:52.369
Maybe stopping it is not what
we should be focusing on.

15:52.452 --> 15:54.537
Do you see her stomach?

15:54.621 --> 15:55.997
Does-- Does any of this
look like a

15:56.081 --> 15:58.500
good fucking thing to you?
What are you talking about?

15:58.583 --> 16:00.877
For all we know, this could be
a temporary side effect. Right?

16:00.960 --> 16:03.004
But what's not temporary
is the fact that someone

16:03.088 --> 16:05.173
who would otherwise be dead is
walking around today

16:05.256 --> 16:07.175
because of what this
allowed Fatima to do, okay?

16:07.258 --> 16:09.052
Can you not see how
this might be helpful?

16:09.135 --> 16:10.970
No! I can't see how it
could be fucking helpful!

16:11.054 --> 16:12.681
-Hey!
-Okay, enough, everybody!

16:12.764 --> 16:15.308
Let's just all take a breath.

16:17.227 --> 16:21.189
Hey, Fatima, I wanna keep
you here for observation.

16:21.272 --> 16:23.983
We can monitor your vitals
and keep an eye out

16:24.067 --> 16:25.694
for any significant changes.

16:25.777 --> 16:27.654
Why don't you go
pack a few things,

16:27.737 --> 16:29.197
enough for a few days,

16:29.280 --> 16:31.032
and we'll take it
from there. Okay?

16:35.620 --> 16:37.455
[Jade] Yeah, there's only one,
one way to enter.

16:37.539 --> 16:40.290
[exhales, groans]

16:40.375 --> 16:42.127
You don't know that; you've only
been down there once!

16:42.210 --> 16:44.170
Yes, and the image
of that chamber

16:44.254 --> 16:46.506
is seared into
my fucking brain!

16:46.589 --> 16:49.551
There's one entrance,
that's it!

16:49.634 --> 16:50.760
There's no version of this

16:50.844 --> 16:52.804
where we go spelunking
and realize, "Oh, hey,

16:52.887 --> 16:55.390
there's a convenient exit
we didn't see before!"

16:55.473 --> 16:57.475
For all we know, they buried
the bones in that chamber

16:57.559 --> 16:59.352
for exactly that reason.

17:00.895 --> 17:02.939
Okay, well,
maybe we could have,

17:03.022 --> 17:04.190
like-- maybe we can find--

17:04.273 --> 17:07.527
Kenny. Kenny, Kenny.
Listen to me. Look.

17:07.609 --> 17:08.944
I say this with love, okay?

17:09.028 --> 17:11.406
You being here right now,
it's not helping.

17:11.489 --> 17:14.992
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.
Yeah, I'm the problem.

17:16.661 --> 17:18.288
Kenny, stop!

17:18.371 --> 17:20.665
Boyd listens to you, okay?

17:20.749 --> 17:23.792
You have to make him realize
that this may not be the kind

17:23.877 --> 17:26.253
of plan where everybody
who goes in comes out.

17:26.337 --> 17:28.173
So, you want me to go back to
Boyd and tell him that he

17:28.256 --> 17:30.717
just needs to accept the fact
that people are gonna die?

17:30.800 --> 17:33.178
-Maybe.
-I'm not doing that.

17:34.971 --> 17:37.182
Well, then, we're not
fucking going home!

17:37.265 --> 17:39.392
There is a reason that no one
has ever gotten out of here,

17:39.476 --> 17:42.228
and maybe that reason is no one
has ever been willing

17:42.312 --> 17:44.314
to make the hard
decisions before!

17:46.024 --> 17:48.151
Let me guess. You're gonna
be one of the people

17:48.234 --> 17:49.652
going down into the tunnels?

17:49.736 --> 17:51.696
Making the hard
decisions?

17:53.865 --> 17:55.325
Yeah.

17:55.408 --> 17:56.951
That's what I thought.

18:11.090 --> 18:12.967
Ahh! Fuck!

18:14.886 --> 18:17.555
[grunts]

18:17.639 --> 18:20.016
You motherfucker! Aah!

18:20.099 --> 18:22.519
[clattering]

18:26.356 --> 18:27.649
[door opens]

18:30.026 --> 18:31.027
Hey.

18:33.321 --> 18:34.531
[door closes]

18:35.573 --> 18:38.243
[sighs] What are you still
doing out here?

18:38.326 --> 18:39.452
[chuckles mirthlessly]

18:43.706 --> 18:45.834
I'm standing here
trying to work up the courage

18:45.917 --> 18:48.044
to tell you the truth.

18:48.127 --> 18:50.463
I, uh...

18:50.547 --> 18:52.549
I lied to you the other day.

18:52.632 --> 18:55.510
You asked me if I was still
seeing things and I said no.

18:56.636 --> 18:57.804
Okay.

18:57.887 --> 18:59.764
It's happening
more frequently...

19:01.850 --> 19:03.560
...seeing things,

19:03.643 --> 19:05.645
hearing things.

19:05.728 --> 19:08.898
I mean, I can't lead this--

19:08.982 --> 19:12.151
I can't lead this place if
I can't trust my own fucking--

19:12.235 --> 19:13.278
come on!

19:13.361 --> 19:16.322
-Boyd? Hey! Look at me.
-I just--

19:16.406 --> 19:18.908
These episodes that
you're talking about,

19:18.992 --> 19:22.370
are they connected
at all to the tremors?

19:22.453 --> 19:24.998
Like-- like are they
happening at the same time?

19:25.081 --> 19:27.041
I-I don't know.
Sometimes, maybe.

19:27.125 --> 19:28.543
I-I haven't really--

19:28.626 --> 19:31.671
Boyd, what aren't
you telling me?

19:33.590 --> 19:36.050
It's all connected to Abby.

19:36.134 --> 19:39.178
Things that I'm seeing,
that I'm hearing.

19:39.262 --> 19:42.932
The other day
I went to her-- her grave.

19:43.016 --> 19:45.935
Her fucking hands came out
of the soil and grabbed me.

19:46.019 --> 19:48.479
-Jesus.
-Look,

19:48.563 --> 19:52.442
I know this place gets into
our heads, but this is--

19:52.525 --> 19:53.818
this is different.

19:55.528 --> 19:56.821
I keep hearing this gunshot.

19:59.866 --> 20:01.701
You never forget the
sound of the shot that--

20:01.784 --> 20:03.745
Hey...

20:03.828 --> 20:06.706
Why is it happening now?
Right?

20:06.789 --> 20:09.208
I can't fall apart, not now,

20:09.292 --> 20:12.045
not when we might be close
to something real. I just...

20:12.128 --> 20:15.673
Okay.
What do you want me to do?

20:17.467 --> 20:19.844
Look, give me a pill.

20:19.928 --> 20:21.220
I don't know.
Give me a Band-Aid, something.

20:21.304 --> 20:23.306
I-- any...

20:23.389 --> 20:26.976
If what Jade says is
right about the bones, then,

20:27.060 --> 20:30.313
I just need to keep it together
a little bit longer.

20:30.396 --> 20:33.816
Please, just--
just give me something

20:33.900 --> 20:36.736
to help me hold it together
a little bit longer.

20:39.197 --> 20:43.743
Boyd, I-I wanna help,
I really do.

20:43.826 --> 20:46.287
But, yeah, I don't think
there's anything that I can do.

20:52.335 --> 20:53.294
Okay.

20:58.675 --> 20:59.801
Hello?

21:03.429 --> 21:04.639
Sheriff Boyd?

21:07.976 --> 21:09.102
Are you here?

21:13.272 --> 21:18.069
[ominous music playing]

21:58.901 --> 22:03.740
[ominous music continues]

22:33.352 --> 22:34.937
Where were you
last night!?

22:35.021 --> 22:37.523
I'm-- I'm so sorry. I, um...

22:37.607 --> 22:39.192
I heard about what
Boyd was planning,

22:39.275 --> 22:42.528
and I just got scared, and I was
already up by the Colony House--

22:42.612 --> 22:43.780
If we're gonna live together,

22:43.863 --> 22:45.364
I need to know where you are
at night.

22:45.448 --> 22:47.283
-You can't just--
-I'm sorry, I...

22:47.366 --> 22:48.409
You've been so nice to me;

22:48.493 --> 22:50.036
I really didn't
mean to worry you.

22:50.119 --> 22:51.662
I swear it won't
happen again.

22:55.374 --> 22:56.709
What's in the bag?

22:58.461 --> 23:01.172
Nothing.
It's just, um...

23:01.255 --> 23:03.257
I'm really tired, okay?

23:03.341 --> 23:05.009
Hey.

23:06.594 --> 23:07.845
What's going on?

23:07.929 --> 23:10.765
They're clothes, okay?

23:10.848 --> 23:13.851
I just thought if I could find
a change of clothes,

23:13.935 --> 23:17.188
then-- then,
I wouldn't feel so...

23:17.271 --> 23:18.689
But then, I realized

23:18.773 --> 23:20.066
that they're all
dead people's clothes,

23:20.149 --> 23:21.359
and none of them fit right,
and I just...

23:24.320 --> 23:25.905
I don't think
I'm doing very well.

23:25.988 --> 23:27.031
Hey.

23:29.909 --> 23:31.661
It's okay.

23:31.744 --> 23:33.704
It's all right.

23:33.788 --> 23:36.040
You must think I'm so weak.

23:36.124 --> 23:38.709
You're actually handling things
a lot better

23:38.793 --> 23:40.419
than I did
when I first got here.

23:40.503 --> 23:41.420
Really?

23:43.089 --> 23:45.007
And I, uh...

23:45.091 --> 23:47.218
know where there's
a great stash of clothes.

23:47.301 --> 23:48.678
So, maybe you and I can go

23:48.761 --> 23:51.389
try some on later together?

23:51.472 --> 23:52.932
I'd really like that.

23:55.560 --> 23:57.353
You're a good
person, Sara.

23:59.272 --> 24:00.857
I'm gonna be at the diner,

24:00.940 --> 24:04.819
helping them sort through the
storage room, if you need me.

24:04.902 --> 24:05.945
Okay.

24:10.783 --> 24:14.662
[ominous music playing]

24:36.309 --> 24:39.270
That morning that I came out
of the root cellar, and...

24:39.353 --> 24:41.731
when I saw that everyone had
died,

24:41.814 --> 24:44.442
that was the first time
I saw the Boy in White.

24:44.525 --> 24:48.654
He told me there were three
things that I would need.

24:48.738 --> 24:50.406
The first was food.

24:52.491 --> 24:54.452
We didn't have all
the stuff that we do now,

24:54.535 --> 24:57.997
like animals and milk
and all that stuff.

24:58.080 --> 25:01.042
So, he brought me here,

25:01.125 --> 25:03.753
and this whole truck

25:03.836 --> 25:07.381
was filled with
canned peaches.

25:07.465 --> 25:10.509
Was that all you had to eat?
Canned peaches?

25:10.593 --> 25:12.511
Sometimes,
I ate other things.

25:12.595 --> 25:14.805
Plants... and bugs;

25:14.889 --> 25:17.016
that was only if I had to.

25:18.434 --> 25:20.478
Come.

25:20.561 --> 25:22.480
I didn't have
a can opener at first,

25:22.563 --> 25:26.234
so I figured out
how to open them

25:26.317 --> 25:28.486
with this rock.

25:28.569 --> 25:30.780
So, you should
hold onto this.

25:33.199 --> 25:34.825
Look.

25:34.909 --> 25:36.202
Yeah.

25:37.995 --> 25:42.792
Ethan, the worst parts
is when you get lonely.

25:42.875 --> 25:46.963
Everything is scarier
when you're lonely.

25:47.046 --> 25:51.133
So, you have to pretend
you're not alone.

25:51.217 --> 25:53.552
That was the second thing
that the Boy in White told me.

25:53.636 --> 25:55.721
And how do you do that?

25:55.805 --> 25:57.723
It was hard at first.
I had to--

25:57.807 --> 25:59.725
I'd make friends with
things on the truck -

25:59.809 --> 26:04.438
the walls and the
floors and the boxes.

26:04.522 --> 26:07.692
I gave them names
and I would talk to them.

26:07.775 --> 26:10.027
But you won't have
to do that, though,

26:10.111 --> 26:14.448
because I thought of
something that's much better.

26:14.532 --> 26:15.908
Okay?

26:15.992 --> 26:17.451
Where are you going?

26:17.535 --> 26:20.621
Just-- Just stay here;
I'm gonna be right back.

26:22.248 --> 26:23.249
[sighs]

26:26.377 --> 26:28.045
Is this helping?

26:28.129 --> 26:29.672
A little, I guess.

26:35.636 --> 26:39.140
I realized that I missed my
mother and Eloise the most.

26:41.642 --> 26:46.564
And so, I found these...

26:46.647 --> 26:48.774
and I dressed them
in their clothes.

26:52.278 --> 26:54.989
And then, for a while,

26:55.072 --> 26:57.950
it felt like that they
were back with me again.

27:00.661 --> 27:03.664
Then, when I--
then when I talked to them,

27:03.748 --> 27:07.084
uh, I could imagine
what they would say back,

27:07.168 --> 27:08.836
and then it didn't
feel as lonely.

27:11.130 --> 27:12.381
But we...
We can change them

27:12.465 --> 27:15.301
into your family.

27:15.384 --> 27:18.095
This could be your... mom

27:18.179 --> 27:20.681
and this could be Julie.

27:20.765 --> 27:22.308
I know it's
a little small, but--

27:22.391 --> 27:26.062
but we could maybe
find something bigger.

27:26.145 --> 27:28.481
I didn't find anything
for your dad, but I thought...

27:28.564 --> 27:29.857
No.
You need to stop it right now.

27:29.940 --> 27:31.067
...we could
make a scarecrow.

27:31.150 --> 27:32.568
You need to stop it
right now, Victor!

27:32.651 --> 27:33.944
What's wrong?

27:34.028 --> 27:36.530
We're done.
We're not doing this anymore.

27:36.614 --> 27:37.573
Stop.

27:40.701 --> 27:42.119
Ethan, listen to me.

27:42.203 --> 27:46.082
You're never
going to be alone.

27:46.165 --> 27:49.335
I will never, ever
let that happen to you.

27:49.418 --> 27:50.628
And I swear to you...

27:52.380 --> 27:53.964
...I'm gonna
get you out of here.

27:56.634 --> 27:58.552
That's what
my mom thought, too.

28:04.517 --> 28:05.643
Where do you want this?

28:05.726 --> 28:07.103
Uh, watches go over there.

28:07.186 --> 28:08.145
Okay.

28:08.229 --> 28:09.814
Oh...

28:09.897 --> 28:11.399
You really are
pretty good at that.

28:11.482 --> 28:14.026
Ah, well, I...
This is nice.

28:14.110 --> 28:16.570
I really appreciate
you letting me help out.

28:16.654 --> 28:18.906
Well, it's important
to keep busy.

28:18.989 --> 28:20.783
It certainly is.

28:20.866 --> 28:22.118
Especially here.

28:22.201 --> 28:23.327
[crashes]

28:28.332 --> 28:30.167
Wha...

28:30.251 --> 28:31.919
[Henry mumbles]

28:32.002 --> 28:36.549
-[Henry mumbles]
-[monitor beeping]

28:36.632 --> 28:38.968
Dad? Dad!

28:39.051 --> 28:40.386
Grandpa's awake again!

28:41.846 --> 28:44.515
[monitor beeping]

28:44.598 --> 28:46.308
Okay.
Get the doctor, quick!

28:46.392 --> 28:47.768
Dad?

28:47.852 --> 28:49.770
Hey, Dad.
Stay with me. Dad.

28:49.854 --> 28:51.772
Vi-- Victor.

28:51.856 --> 28:53.441
Yeah.

28:53.524 --> 28:55.651
What-- what's happening?

28:55.734 --> 28:57.445
Hey, Dad,
you're in a care facility.

28:57.528 --> 28:59.280
Where... I am in a--

28:59.363 --> 29:03.159
what? No, I was...

29:03.242 --> 29:06.579
I was in the diner,
where I was chopping vegetables.

29:06.662 --> 29:09.707
No, Dad, it wasn't real.

29:09.790 --> 29:12.918
I need you to
listen to me, okay?

29:13.919 --> 29:16.881
And this might not
be easy for you to hear.

29:16.964 --> 29:18.424
A long time ago,

29:18.507 --> 29:21.093
Mom surprised you
on your birthday.

29:21.177 --> 29:23.679
She came home with
two hits of acid.

29:23.762 --> 29:24.889
Do you remember that?

29:24.972 --> 29:26.182
Of course I remember.

29:26.265 --> 29:27.933
Okay.

29:28.017 --> 29:30.853
Well,
there was a problem.

29:30.936 --> 29:32.813
There was something
wrong with the drugs,

29:32.897 --> 29:36.609
and you had
a really bad reaction,

29:36.692 --> 29:39.862
and it was like you just--
you weren't there anymore,

29:39.945 --> 29:42.656
and you've been
in this facility ever since.

29:44.366 --> 29:48.412
Who-- Who was that boy?

29:48.496 --> 29:50.789
That's--
That's my son,

29:50.873 --> 29:53.959
Sebastian.
That's your grandson.

29:55.044 --> 29:57.463
I...
I have a grandson?

29:57.546 --> 29:59.173
Yeah.

29:59.256 --> 30:00.966
You're gonna
stay with us, okay?

30:01.050 --> 30:03.844
I just spoke to Eloise,

30:03.928 --> 30:05.804
and she's
getting on a plane,

30:05.888 --> 30:07.890
and she's flying out
to see you right now.

30:07.973 --> 30:11.060
Eloise? She's alive?

30:11.143 --> 30:12.853
Of course she's alive.

30:12.937 --> 30:14.021
[weeping]

30:14.104 --> 30:16.565
Do you know she's
a school teacher?

30:16.649 --> 30:19.026
A school t...

30:19.109 --> 30:22.112
[monitor beeping]

30:22.196 --> 30:26.659
No, no,
it can't be happening.

30:26.742 --> 30:28.994
This-- no, no,
it can't be real.

30:29.078 --> 30:31.372
Dad, Dad,
you have to stay with me.

30:31.455 --> 30:34.375
[voice echoing]
No, Dad, stay with me.

30:34.458 --> 30:35.376
Please?

30:39.004 --> 30:41.590
[Sarah] Here.
Let me help you with that.

30:41.674 --> 30:42.758
[Bakta] Oh...

30:48.138 --> 30:49.890
You okay?

30:54.687 --> 30:57.982
Uh, I think, uh...

30:59.275 --> 31:02.319
I appreciate you letting me
help, but I think I need to go.

31:05.489 --> 31:07.575
Hey, I'm gonna
head back down to--

31:09.493 --> 31:11.245
What are you doing?

31:11.328 --> 31:13.664
I'm gonna stay
with you at the clinic.

31:13.747 --> 31:15.499
You don't
have to do that.

31:15.583 --> 31:18.085
Yeah, I know. I just...
don't want you to be alone.

31:18.168 --> 31:20.296
That's not
why you're coming.

31:22.881 --> 31:24.842
I don't understand
how could she say

31:24.925 --> 31:27.303
that any of this could
possibly be a good thing.

31:28.762 --> 31:30.472
What if it is?

31:30.556 --> 31:33.100
-What? Are you serious?
-Ellis, I was so freaked out;

31:33.183 --> 31:36.103
it didn't
even occur to me.

31:36.186 --> 31:38.439
I connected
with that thing.

31:38.522 --> 31:40.774
I controlled it.

31:40.858 --> 31:43.611
If there is a way
I can figure out how to use that

31:43.694 --> 31:45.863
to help us,
why wouldn't I even try?

31:45.946 --> 31:47.906
I understand how you feel,
but that is not--

31:47.990 --> 31:50.868
No, you don't.
I'm sorry.

31:50.951 --> 31:52.620
With everything's
that's happened,

31:52.703 --> 31:54.955
you have no idea how it
feels to feel that powerless

31:55.039 --> 31:57.041
in a place like this,

31:57.124 --> 31:58.667
to feel like you're at the mercy

31:58.751 --> 32:00.711
of these things that have
gotten inside your head,

32:00.794 --> 32:02.546
gotten inside my body!

32:02.630 --> 32:05.633
That thing was inside me.
Can you honestly stand there

32:05.716 --> 32:07.092
and tell me you know
how that feels?

32:09.261 --> 32:10.554
No.

32:10.638 --> 32:11.764
And now, I may finally

32:11.847 --> 32:13.599
have a way that
I can take back control,

32:13.682 --> 32:16.185
that I can fight back,

32:16.268 --> 32:18.020
something that could
actually help us go home!

32:18.103 --> 32:19.688
And you want me
to ignore that?

32:19.772 --> 32:21.315
No, I want you to acknowledge
what this thing

32:21.398 --> 32:22.775
might actually
fucking do to you!

32:22.858 --> 32:24.026
I don't care what
it does to me!

32:24.109 --> 32:25.819
I fucking care!

32:25.903 --> 32:27.363
If I lose you...

32:28.947 --> 32:32.576
there is no... home
for me to go to anymore.

32:34.578 --> 32:35.996
Ellis...

32:37.915 --> 32:39.291
Ah, shit.

32:43.253 --> 32:45.130
I understand that
you wanna help,

32:45.214 --> 32:47.466
[sniffles]

32:47.549 --> 32:50.427
and I want you to feel like
you have control again,

32:50.511 --> 32:52.388
but it's...

32:56.475 --> 32:58.727
This shit is scaring
the hell outta me.

33:01.855 --> 33:02.940
[exhaling sharply]

33:10.447 --> 33:14.618
Look, the truth is,

33:14.702 --> 33:16.245
what you're afraid of...

33:16.328 --> 33:19.289
it may already
be happening.

33:19.373 --> 33:22.501
And if-- if it is,

33:23.794 --> 33:27.089
then I need to be able to
take what good I can from that.

33:30.843 --> 33:32.010
Yeah.

33:43.230 --> 33:44.148
Hey.

33:44.231 --> 33:45.315
Hey.

33:45.399 --> 33:46.734
Can I talk to you?

33:46.817 --> 33:48.193
Of course.

33:48.277 --> 33:51.029
What was that back there?

33:51.113 --> 33:53.782
What you said to Fatima
was way outta line.

33:53.866 --> 33:57.244
What-- are you kidding me?

33:57.327 --> 33:59.538
We have no idea
what's happening to her.

33:59.621 --> 34:01.457
She's terrified.

34:01.540 --> 34:03.167
That was not the time or
place to go off like that.

34:03.250 --> 34:04.585
Not the time or place? Kristi,

34:04.668 --> 34:06.962
she saved someone's life.

34:07.045 --> 34:09.130
Why am I the only person
who sees the value in that?

34:09.214 --> 34:11.091
I'm not saying
there's no value to it.

34:11.175 --> 34:12.634
Then, what
are you saying?

34:12.717 --> 34:14.011
Jesus, there are things

34:14.094 --> 34:16.889
that come out of the woods
at night to hunt us.

34:16.972 --> 34:19.558
We need to be finding every
advantage we possibly can.

34:19.641 --> 34:22.018
I'm sorry if my timing
was inappropriate.

34:22.101 --> 34:25.563
I'm saying that we need
to be careful, okay?

34:25.647 --> 34:27.232
This place has
a way of making you think

34:27.315 --> 34:28.859
you're doing good things,

34:28.942 --> 34:30.819
things that
you think will help.

34:30.902 --> 34:32.321
Yeah, it also has a way of

34:32.404 --> 34:33.739
making you terrified
to do anything.

34:36.492 --> 34:38.494
Kristi,
I want us to go home.

34:38.577 --> 34:40.913
I want us to live the life
that we were supposed to have.

34:42.498 --> 34:44.081
So, do I.

34:44.166 --> 34:46.001
Then, what are we
arguing about?

34:48.670 --> 34:51.757
Look, I-I know
we're all scared.

34:51.840 --> 34:53.926
I'm fucking terrified.

34:54.009 --> 34:56.678
But we have no idea what
is happening to Fatima,

34:56.762 --> 34:59.014
and I'm not willing
to risk her safety

34:59.097 --> 35:00.641
so that I feel less afraid.

35:00.724 --> 35:01.850
Kristi--

35:01.934 --> 35:04.812
She is my patient,
she's under my care;

35:04.895 --> 35:07.022
if you have something to say
to her, you go through me.

35:15.030 --> 35:17.491
Yeah, just, uh,
let me know

35:17.574 --> 35:19.868
if you want me to change
any more sheets or anything.

35:21.036 --> 35:22.788
[exhales]

35:26.834 --> 35:29.461
"There's only
one way in or out."

35:29.545 --> 35:32.256
[sighs]

35:32.339 --> 35:35.467
"That's a shooting gallery.
I was in the army."

35:52.734 --> 35:53.694
[gasps]

35:55.237 --> 35:56.905
Holy shit.

35:59.157 --> 36:00.784
Boyd?

36:00.868 --> 36:02.119
[Boyd] In here.

36:07.165 --> 36:08.917
What's going on?

36:09.001 --> 36:11.962
Someone was in here.

36:12.045 --> 36:14.590
Are you sure?

36:14.673 --> 36:17.634
Yeah, I'm sure.
The yellow suit is gone.

36:17.718 --> 36:19.970
What?

36:20.053 --> 36:22.514
I got tired of staring
at the goddamn thing,

36:22.598 --> 36:25.475
so I put it in here,

36:25.559 --> 36:27.811
or... I thought I did.

36:27.895 --> 36:29.730
Why would someone come in here
just to take the yellow suit?

36:29.813 --> 36:31.189
I don't know, Kenny.

36:31.273 --> 36:32.983
Maybe the guy it
belonged to got tired

36:33.066 --> 36:35.611
of walking around naked
in the woods. I don't know.

36:35.694 --> 36:37.779
Do you think maybe Victor
or Henry might have taken it?

36:37.863 --> 36:39.364
[Jade] Boyd!

36:41.700 --> 36:43.660
Boyd! Hey!

36:45.037 --> 36:46.371
Did you take the suit?

36:46.455 --> 36:48.498
-The what?
-The yellow suit,

36:48.582 --> 36:49.875
it's gone.

36:49.958 --> 36:52.586
Forget the suit!
I got it! I fucking got it!

36:52.669 --> 36:54.880
I know how we're getting in
and out of the cavern!

36:54.963 --> 36:56.214
Okay.

36:56.298 --> 36:59.551
-The Bottle Tree!
-What?

36:59.635 --> 37:01.219
Just come!
Come with me!

37:05.057 --> 37:06.350
Hello?

37:08.143 --> 37:12.981
[ominous music playing]

37:32.668 --> 37:37.506
[ominous music continues]

37:57.484 --> 37:59.319
Ethan, let's go.

37:59.403 --> 38:02.864
We can't.
We're not done yet.

38:02.948 --> 38:04.825
Listen, Jade and Boyd

38:04.908 --> 38:07.536
are working on a plan
right now to help us get home.

38:07.619 --> 38:08.620
Come on.

38:08.704 --> 38:10.664
But what if it doesn't?

38:10.747 --> 38:12.708
Miranda thought she
would get everybody home,

38:12.791 --> 38:14.167
but then everybody died.

38:14.251 --> 38:16.545
How do you know the same thing
won't happen again?

38:17.629 --> 38:18.714
[sighs]

38:22.884 --> 38:25.762
Because...

38:25.846 --> 38:27.973
things are
different this time.

38:28.056 --> 38:29.850
We know things now.

38:29.933 --> 38:32.144
Jade and I...

38:32.227 --> 38:34.980
we have memories that
Miranda didn't have.

38:38.191 --> 38:40.777
She tried, Victor.

38:40.861 --> 38:42.696
She tried so hard.

38:42.779 --> 38:46.158
I know because
I feel what she felt.

38:50.037 --> 38:51.580
I know how much
she loved you.

38:53.832 --> 38:56.376
I know how badly she
wanted to take you home.

38:58.920 --> 39:00.047
She just...

39:00.130 --> 39:02.340
didn't have
the answers she needed.

39:08.930 --> 39:10.766
But I do.

39:12.768 --> 39:15.437
I have them because of her.

39:15.520 --> 39:18.231
She's the one that
led me to the tower,

39:18.315 --> 39:20.275
to your father.

39:23.361 --> 39:26.073
She's the reason
why you get to go home.

39:26.156 --> 39:27.699
What?

39:30.827 --> 39:34.039
I don't think I came back
just to free the children.

39:37.959 --> 39:42.255
I came back for you, Victor.

39:42.339 --> 39:44.800
I'm gonna take you home.

39:52.349 --> 39:54.017
So, we're gonna
go to town now.

40:01.525 --> 40:04.528
And we're not gonna
draw any more pictures

40:04.611 --> 40:09.074
because neither of you are
ever going to be alone again.

40:10.659 --> 40:11.952
I promise.

40:35.851 --> 40:38.311
You see, the whole-- the whole
time, I've been focusing on

40:38.395 --> 40:40.272
the entrances and
exits that are there now.

40:40.355 --> 40:42.107
But what I should
have been thinking about

40:42.190 --> 40:43.900
was the exit that
used to be there!

40:43.984 --> 40:45.193
What are you
talking about?

40:45.277 --> 40:47.779
There was a fucking
hole in the ceiling!

40:47.863 --> 40:49.197
And there were these roots

40:49.281 --> 40:51.658
that formed the symbol--
uh, you remember the symbol.

40:51.741 --> 40:53.243
Yeah.

40:53.326 --> 40:54.995
Victor said--

40:55.078 --> 40:56.913
Victor said those
roots became a tree.

40:58.039 --> 40:59.291
This tree.

41:02.961 --> 41:07.174
Gentlemen,
we are, at this moment,

41:07.257 --> 41:09.426
standing right
above the cavern

41:09.509 --> 41:12.929
those bones
are buried in.

41:13.013 --> 41:15.724
You said we couldn't go into the
tunnels without a second exit,

41:15.807 --> 41:17.517
so let's make one.

41:17.601 --> 41:21.271
Wha...? You...
You wanna cut down the tree?

41:21.354 --> 41:24.316
I wanna
pull it out by the roots.

41:24.399 --> 41:26.026
And before you say
that's impossible,

41:26.109 --> 41:28.195
there is a clearing about
a hundred yards from here;

41:28.278 --> 41:30.030
the road isn't too far
from that clearing.

41:30.113 --> 41:31.865
We get the truck and
the van in there, we use--

41:31.948 --> 41:33.366
we use every inch
of chain we have,

41:33.450 --> 41:35.702
we get some leverage from the
other trees, we do it right,

41:35.785 --> 41:37.704
it'll be like pulling a stopper
out of a bottle.

41:37.787 --> 41:39.331
[makes popping sound]
Think about it.

41:39.414 --> 41:41.833
We send one team down there
while those things are asleep,

41:41.917 --> 41:43.752
they get to the chamber,
block the entrance,

41:43.835 --> 41:45.629
they put a talisman
up for good measure;

41:45.712 --> 41:47.255
and while they dig
for the bones,

41:47.339 --> 41:49.507
there's another team
up here working on the tree.

41:49.591 --> 41:51.676
By the time the bones are
dug up, the tree is out.

41:51.760 --> 41:54.095
We lift everyone up to safety,
get back to town,

41:54.179 --> 41:56.973
we're behind closed
doors by sunset. Easy peasy.

41:59.601 --> 42:02.687
Boyd, that--
that could work.

42:02.771 --> 42:03.939
Boyd?

42:05.482 --> 42:08.151
What happens...

42:08.235 --> 42:09.819
when the first
group is down there,

42:09.903 --> 42:11.905
and the tree
doesn't come out?

42:11.988 --> 42:13.698
What happens
if the chain breaks

42:13.782 --> 42:16.201
or-or if we don't
have enough leverage?

42:16.284 --> 42:17.744
That's never gonna happen.

42:17.827 --> 42:20.080
Wait.
You know that for sure?

42:20.163 --> 42:22.916
Because what
I wanna know is what's plan B

42:22.999 --> 42:24.334
when the tree doesn't
come out

42:24.417 --> 42:25.919
and we have five
or six people

42:26.002 --> 42:28.964
barricaded in a death trap
with no place else to go?

42:29.047 --> 42:30.298
Plan B?

42:30.382 --> 42:31.758
[Boyd] Yeah.

42:31.841 --> 42:33.009
[exhales]

42:34.886 --> 42:37.305
You-You asked for a solution
to an impossible problem.

42:37.389 --> 42:40.058
I am serving it to you
on a goddamn platter!

42:40.141 --> 42:41.726
Now, you're asking
for a plan B?

42:41.810 --> 42:43.478
-That's right.
-All right, okay--

42:43.561 --> 42:47.482
No! Let me make this as clear
as I can possibly can.

42:47.565 --> 42:49.901
I am not sending people
down into those tunnels

42:49.985 --> 42:51.820
with nothing
but a hope and a prayer

42:51.903 --> 42:54.906
that we pull the magic tree
out by its roots!

42:54.990 --> 42:57.075
Landscaping is not a plan!

42:58.493 --> 43:00.287
Landscaping. Fuck you!

43:00.370 --> 43:02.038
Great! We're done here!

43:06.084 --> 43:08.253
Hey, just--
just give him some time.

43:10.463 --> 43:12.215
[chuckles]
"Landscaping".

43:13.967 --> 43:16.803
[crow cawing in distance]

43:19.764 --> 43:20.890
[Kenny] Boyd?

43:20.974 --> 43:22.517
Hey, over here!

43:23.977 --> 43:25.478
-Oh.
-[gun firing]

43:25.562 --> 43:26.980
[gasps]

43:27.063 --> 43:28.106
Kenny!

43:29.441 --> 43:31.401
Kenny! No!

43:31.484 --> 43:32.777
Hey. No, no, no, no. Hey!

43:32.861 --> 43:34.529
Don't-- don't talk, okay?

43:34.612 --> 43:36.573
Hold on, Buddy!

43:36.656 --> 43:38.325
Kenny. Hey, look!

43:38.408 --> 43:40.035
Look at me.

43:40.118 --> 43:41.786
Kenny! Kenny!

43:41.870 --> 43:42.996
Hey!

43:43.079 --> 43:45.123
God damn it!

43:56.051 --> 43:57.177
Uh...

43:57.260 --> 43:58.678
[breathing rapidly]

43:58.762 --> 44:03.641
[suspenseful music plays]

44:06.436 --> 44:08.938
[stammering]

44:09.022 --> 44:10.815
[groaning]

44:10.899 --> 44:12.692
Ah...

44:12.776 --> 44:13.860
Ah...

44:19.616 --> 44:20.867
Abby?

44:26.122 --> 44:27.207
[choking]

44:27.290 --> 44:28.333
Oh!

44:28.416 --> 44:29.334
Oh, shit!

44:32.087 --> 44:34.089
[stammering]

44:34.172 --> 44:35.882
God!

44:35.965 --> 44:40.387
What the fuck
do you want from me?!

44:40.470 --> 44:42.097
Huh?!

45:01.825 --> 45:03.368
I don't know
how much sense it makes

45:03.451 --> 45:04.911
for me to be
standing here right now.

45:07.038 --> 45:09.916
You were always
the spiritual one,

45:09.999 --> 45:11.751
the smart one.

45:11.835 --> 45:13.044
[exhaling sharply]

45:14.921 --> 45:18.675
These things
I'm-- I'm seeing...

45:18.758 --> 45:20.593
could they be real?

45:22.220 --> 45:24.013
Did I really have it...

45:24.097 --> 45:27.350
wrong this whole time?

45:27.434 --> 45:29.686
[exhaling sharply]

45:29.769 --> 45:32.605
Well, it seems like me getting
my brain fried on that acid

45:32.689 --> 45:36.151
makes a whole lot
more sense than-- than,

45:36.234 --> 45:37.694
well-- any of this.

45:41.698 --> 45:47.036
Everything's
so... nice... there,

45:47.120 --> 45:50.248
in that place I've seen.

45:50.331 --> 45:53.168
Victor, he...
[chuckles]

45:53.251 --> 45:55.962
...he wears a shirt and tie.

45:56.045 --> 46:00.258
And then,
we... have... a grandson.

46:00.341 --> 46:03.678
He-- He has your eyes.

46:03.761 --> 46:06.055
And Eloise...

46:06.139 --> 46:07.140
...you're not--

46:07.223 --> 46:10.059
you're on a plane.

46:10.143 --> 46:14.397
You're on a plane, and...

46:14.481 --> 46:16.483
I don't know where
it's coming from,

46:16.566 --> 46:19.027
but I'm gonna
ask the next time I...

46:19.110 --> 46:20.737
[weeping]

46:22.405 --> 46:23.656
Oh...

46:23.740 --> 46:28.119
Could I
really be so lost?

46:28.203 --> 46:31.706
All that time...

46:31.789 --> 46:34.459
Or...

46:34.542 --> 46:37.378
did I come all this way,

46:37.462 --> 46:41.799
so that I could finally...

46:41.883 --> 46:43.176
go home?

46:46.262 --> 46:48.723
If that's true...

46:48.806 --> 46:52.227
help me. Help me.

46:52.310 --> 46:54.395
-Please help me.
-[Joni Mitchell "Blue" playing]

46:54.479 --> 46:56.439
[monitor beeping]
-What?

46:56.523 --> 47:00.610
-[monitor beeping]
-[Joni Mitchell "Blue" playing]

47:00.693 --> 47:04.614
♪ Blue... ♪

47:04.697 --> 47:05.657
Dad.

47:05.740 --> 47:07.659
[murmur]

47:07.742 --> 47:09.035
It's working.

47:09.118 --> 47:10.912
♪ Songs are like tattoos ♪

47:10.995 --> 47:12.247
Hey, Dad.

47:12.330 --> 47:14.874
That was your song, remember?

47:14.958 --> 47:18.670
Yeah. Lots of laughs.

47:18.753 --> 47:21.422
♪ Crown and anchor me ♪

47:21.506 --> 47:22.465
[doctor]
Henry?

47:22.549 --> 47:25.093
♪ Or let me sail away ♪

47:25.176 --> 47:28.179
I need you to focus.
You're getting stronger.

47:28.263 --> 47:29.347
You're coming back now more

47:29.430 --> 47:31.558
than you have
in a very long time.

47:31.641 --> 47:33.142
But if you want to stay,

47:33.226 --> 47:35.311
there's something
you need to do.

47:35.395 --> 47:37.230
Do you want
to stay here, Henry?

47:37.313 --> 47:39.357
Yes. Yes.

47:39.440 --> 47:42.443
-[Joni Mitchell "Blue" playing]
-Yes, I do.

47:42.527 --> 47:43.319
[doctor] Good.

47:45.113 --> 47:47.782
Then, you have to do
exactly as I tell you.

47:47.865 --> 47:49.284
Okay.

47:49.367 --> 47:51.244
You see, the mind craves
what is familiar.

47:51.327 --> 47:53.413
And you have lived
in this delusion for so long

47:53.496 --> 47:56.249
that your mind
believes that it's real.

47:56.332 --> 47:58.585
Just telling yourself
that it's not won't be enough.

48:00.086 --> 48:02.797
You have to forcibly disconnect

48:02.880 --> 48:05.758
from whatever is anchoring you
to that version of reality.

48:07.343 --> 48:08.553
How?

48:08.636 --> 48:11.014
You have to
eliminate the anchor.

48:11.097 --> 48:14.601
♪ Lots of laughs-- ♪

48:14.684 --> 48:16.352
What happened?

48:16.436 --> 48:17.895
I lost service.

48:17.979 --> 48:19.480
[voice echoing]
Henry? Henry.

48:22.358 --> 48:24.152
What?

48:24.235 --> 48:25.445
No!

48:26.571 --> 48:28.197
No, please, come back.

48:28.281 --> 48:29.824
[stammers]
What did you mean?

48:29.907 --> 48:32.577
How do I forcibly disconnect?

48:32.660 --> 48:34.495
What--

48:34.579 --> 48:37.332
Miranda, please!

48:37.415 --> 48:40.668
[whimpering]
Help me go back!

48:40.752 --> 48:42.670
Please?

48:42.754 --> 48:45.048
Please!

48:45.131 --> 48:46.966
What? Where am I?

48:47.050 --> 48:50.011
[stammering]

48:50.094 --> 48:53.139
[weeping]

49:06.611 --> 49:10.156
Any, um...
Any dizziness?

49:10.239 --> 49:11.199
No.

49:11.282 --> 49:12.533
Shortness of breath?

49:12.617 --> 49:13.618
[Fatima] No.

49:13.701 --> 49:15.286
[Kristi]
Light-headedness?

49:15.370 --> 49:16.537
Not really.

49:16.621 --> 49:18.623
[Kristi]
Any pain?

49:18.706 --> 49:21.542
Aside from the marks,
I'm fine.

49:21.626 --> 49:23.628
That cold sensation
you talked about before...

49:23.711 --> 49:24.962
It's gone.

49:27.507 --> 49:29.717
That thing you said earlier

49:29.801 --> 49:34.097
about being maybe
able to control this,

49:34.180 --> 49:35.848
do you really think
that's possible?

49:35.932 --> 49:38.476
Uh, it's hard to say.

49:38.559 --> 49:40.978
But you must
have had some idea.

49:43.106 --> 49:45.441
I think there's a couple of
things we could try, yeah.

49:45.525 --> 49:47.985
Can I talk to you?

49:48.069 --> 49:49.654
Out there.

49:56.160 --> 49:57.245
Enough.

49:57.328 --> 49:58.663
Okay? Enough.
You heard her.

49:58.746 --> 50:00.456
She wants to do this.
She wants to try.

50:00.540 --> 50:02.792
Are you really gonna tell her
that she can't use what's hap--

50:02.875 --> 50:05.878
Her blood pressure
is 53 over 33.

50:05.962 --> 50:07.880
What?

50:07.964 --> 50:11.968
Her heart rate
is 19 beats per minute.

50:12.051 --> 50:13.428
That's impossible.

50:13.511 --> 50:14.804
I know. I checked twice.

50:14.887 --> 50:16.556
I mean, medically speaking,

50:16.639 --> 50:18.099
Fatima shouldn't
even be alive right now.

50:18.182 --> 50:21.102
[ominous music playing]

50:29.193 --> 50:31.237
Mom, is it okay

50:31.320 --> 50:33.364
if we go up to Colony House
and check in on Donna?

50:36.826 --> 50:39.162
I think she'd like that.

50:39.245 --> 50:40.580
Go ahead.
I'll meet you there.

50:56.053 --> 50:59.056
[phone ringing]

50:59.140 --> 51:02.018
[ominous music playing]

51:02.101 --> 51:05.897
[phone ringing]

51:11.027 --> 51:12.820
[phone ringing]

51:19.786 --> 51:22.330
[phone ringing]

51:22.413 --> 51:24.749
[static buzzing]

51:26.751 --> 51:28.377
Hello?

51:28.461 --> 51:30.546
[Thomas]
Mom? It's Thomas.

51:30.630 --> 51:33.508
[static buzzing]

51:33.591 --> 51:35.468
Aren't you
gonna say anything?

51:35.551 --> 51:37.470
[static buzzing]

51:40.431 --> 51:42.725
What do you want?

51:42.809 --> 51:44.644
Come to the RV,

51:44.727 --> 51:46.646
or I'll hurt
Julie and Ethan.

51:46.729 --> 51:51.526
[static buzzing]

51:51.609 --> 51:53.110
[ominous music playing]

51:59.867 --> 52:01.661
You know no version
of Jade's plan

52:01.744 --> 52:03.454
is ever gonna be
good enough for you, right?

52:03.538 --> 52:05.122
Look, I'm not
fucking talking to you.

52:09.544 --> 52:10.586
Look--

52:10.670 --> 52:13.589
No! God, no!
Ya hear me?

52:13.673 --> 52:15.466
I've had enough,
all right?!

52:15.550 --> 52:17.635
You got something to tell me,
then fucking tell me!

52:17.718 --> 52:19.595
All right.

52:21.639 --> 52:23.224
You need to get over it.

52:23.307 --> 52:24.892
Excuse me?

52:24.976 --> 52:27.562
You need to get over the fact
that you killed your wife.

52:27.645 --> 52:29.188
You need to accept
that you did what you did

52:29.272 --> 52:31.023
because it was the
only choice you had,

52:31.107 --> 52:33.401
and nothing you did that morning
could have saved her.

52:37.989 --> 52:40.867
Just like you need
to accept the fact that,

52:40.950 --> 52:42.410
no matter how
great your plan is,

52:42.493 --> 52:44.954
you're probably gonna lose
people going into those tunnels.

52:45.037 --> 52:47.874
-Is that right?
-Oh, yeah.

52:47.957 --> 52:50.459
You're not in peace time
anymore, Boyd.

52:50.543 --> 52:54.088
This isn't about keeping
everybody safe and sound.

52:54.171 --> 52:57.425
I mean, you think this
place pushed back before?

52:57.508 --> 52:59.427
No, Boyd. Look at me.

53:01.512 --> 53:03.973
This is it.

53:04.056 --> 53:07.560
This is where
you make your stand.

53:07.643 --> 53:09.270
And it's not about
saving everyone;

53:09.353 --> 53:11.647
it's about saving
as many as you can.

53:13.149 --> 53:14.400
When you shot Abby,

53:14.483 --> 53:17.361
you saved Ellis.

53:17.445 --> 53:20.573
You go down in those tunnels,
collect those bones, yeah,

53:20.656 --> 53:23.034
you're probably
gonna lose some people,

53:23.117 --> 53:26.329
but you could save
a whole lot more.

53:26.412 --> 53:29.624
So, suck it up,
make a choice and live with it.

53:31.500 --> 53:33.711
[growls, shouts]

53:38.049 --> 53:40.134
[shouts]

53:56.192 --> 53:57.693
Hello?

53:59.654 --> 54:01.572
[ominous music playing]

54:16.045 --> 54:19.256
Thanks for coming.

54:19.340 --> 54:21.968
I wasn't sure
you would.

54:22.051 --> 54:24.887
You know who I am?

54:26.305 --> 54:27.223
Oh.

54:29.350 --> 54:32.144
You haven't remembered
that part yet.

54:32.228 --> 54:33.771
You know...

54:33.854 --> 54:36.148
your husband died
right where you're standing.

54:39.402 --> 54:40.695
Jim was so brave.

54:43.155 --> 54:45.282
I really liked him.

54:45.366 --> 54:47.326
I kept one of his teeth,
you know?

54:50.329 --> 54:51.956
Did you bring me
here to kill me?

54:52.039 --> 54:53.708
Kill you?

54:53.791 --> 54:55.543
Heaven's no.

54:55.626 --> 54:58.045
We've been through
so much together, you and I.

55:00.381 --> 55:03.259
You're as close
to a friend as I ever had.

55:03.342 --> 55:05.928
You and Jade,

55:06.012 --> 55:08.347
you're doing
so well this time.

55:08.431 --> 55:09.932
I wouldn't dream
of killing you.

55:11.267 --> 55:12.435
Not yet.

55:15.896 --> 55:18.149
-Then, why am I here?
-You're here

55:18.232 --> 55:19.692
because you're about
to do something

55:19.775 --> 55:21.318
you've never done before.

55:21.402 --> 55:24.030
We've played
this game so many times...

55:24.113 --> 55:25.448
[gasps]

55:25.531 --> 55:28.701
...but the notion of you
digging up those bones?

55:28.784 --> 55:30.369
Oh...

55:30.453 --> 55:34.290
You may have
finally found the key

55:34.373 --> 55:36.500
to setting
those children free,

55:36.584 --> 55:39.920
to bringing your
own children home.

55:40.004 --> 55:41.172
Or...

55:41.255 --> 55:44.133
you're about to unleash

55:44.216 --> 55:48.637
a type of suffering you
can't even begin to imagine.

55:50.514 --> 55:52.058
[gasps]

55:54.101 --> 55:55.019
[chuckles]

55:56.270 --> 55:57.938
This was really nice.

55:59.398 --> 56:00.691
I really have
missed you.

56:03.903 --> 56:05.571
I'll see you soon.

56:07.198 --> 56:08.157
[kissing]

56:10.576 --> 56:13.287
[humming a tune]

56:15.331 --> 56:17.166
[humming a tune]

56:17.249 --> 56:19.001
[ominous music playing]

56:24.048 --> 56:24.965
Oh, my God.

56:31.722 --> 56:33.641
[theme music playing]
